update public.project_contacts set
  linkedin_connect_message = $$Hi Mark, congratulations on joining Restaurant365. Your mandate to build on the brand and help more operators discover R365 stood out. I build growth systems that connect positioning, customer intelligence, marketing, and RevOps. I would value connecting.$$,
  intro_message = $$Thanks for connecting, Mark. Based on your work as Chief Marketing Officer at Restaurant365, I wanted to be direct about why I reached out. RevHub helps organizations connect customer and market intelligence, segmentation, pricing, marketing, sales execution, operations, forecasting and executive reporting into one commercial growth system. For Restaurant365, the opportunity I see is: RevHub can help Mark connect market positioning, segmentation, demand generation, customer data, lifecycle measurement, and revenue operations so marketing scales as part of one commercial system. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss what we do and whether it could support your priorities?$$,
  follow_up_message = $$Hi Mark, following up in case my earlier note got buried. I outlined the commercial growth approach behind RevHub here: https://aboutchad.com/approach. Based on your role at Restaurant365, I believe there may be a relevant opportunity around new cmo joining during a growth and market-expansion phase while r365 broadens its ai platform and revenue operations capability. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss the approach and whether it could be useful to your team?$$,
  email_subject = $$A faster way to connect R365's growth story to revenue$$,
  email_intro_message = $$Hi Mark,

I saw Restaurant365's continued investment in marketing, RevOps, AI, and customer growth. The opportunity is bigger than adding campaigns or reporting. It is creating one commercial system that connects market positioning, restaurant segments, acquisition, sales conversion, implementation, product adoption, retention, and expansion.

I have spent more than 15 years building that connective layer. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while joining fragmented CRM, marketing, customer, call-center, and operational data into a usable growth model. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I bring the strategy, analytics, and execution capacity needed to accelerate the work without forcing the company to hire several separate specialists.

For R365, I would start by mapping the buyer and customer lifecycle by segment, identifying where messaging, data, ownership, and measurement break, then turning that into a prioritized growth and operating roadmap.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation next week? My approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$,
  email_follow_up_1 = $$Hi Mark,

One practical first deliverable would be a segment-level growth map connecting acquisition source, opportunity creation, implementation, adoption, retention, and expansion. It would show where growth is slowing, which handoffs are creating friction, and which marketing investments are producing durable revenue rather than surface-level activity.

Would Tuesday or Wednesday be easier for a brief discussion?$$,
  email_follow_up_2 = $$Hi Mark,

Closing the loop in case this is relevant to your current planning. I can share a concise first-30-days framework for connecting R365's positioning, demand engine, lifecycle data, and revenue measurement.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding, or is someone else on your team better suited for the conversation?$$,
  email_assumption_notice = $$Assumed from the first-initial-plus-last-name pattern demonstrated by tsmith@restaurant365.com. This email may not work and should be verified before sending.$$
where lower(contact_name) = lower('Mark Grilli') and company = 'Restaurant365';

update public.project_contacts set
  linkedin_connect_message = $$Hi Helene, your perspective on eliminating RevOps silos and aligning forecasting from the field through the C-suite resonated with me. I build commercial growth systems across data, process, analytics, and activation. I would value connecting.$$,
  intro_message = $$Thanks for connecting, Helene. Based on your work as Vice President, Revenue Operations & Enablement at Restaurant365, I wanted to be direct about why I reached out. RevHub helps organizations connect customer and market intelligence, segmentation, pricing, marketing, sales execution, operations, forecasting and executive reporting into one commercial growth system. For Restaurant365, the opportunity I see is: RevHub can expand Helene's internal RevOps capacity with a fractional commercial strategy and data team that accelerates cross-functional design, analytics, and implementation without adding several separate hires. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss what we do and whether it could support your priorities?$$,
  follow_up_message = $$Hi Helene, following up in case my earlier note got buried. I outlined the commercial growth approach behind RevHub here: https://aboutchad.com/approach. Based on your role at Restaurant365, I believe there may be a relevant opportunity around revops leader publicly focused on eliminating silos, aligning forecasting from sellers through the c-suite, improving data hygiene, and scaling tam, territory, channel, and ai-enabled processes. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss the approach and whether it could be useful to your team?$$,
  email_subject = $$Closing the gap between RevOps strategy and execution at R365$$,
  email_intro_message = $$Hi Helene,

Your public perspective on eliminating RevOps silos and aligning forecasting from the field through the C-suite stood out. Restaurant365 appears to be building the right capabilities, but the hardest work often sits between the strategy and the systems: shared lifecycle definitions, account and territory logic, clean source data, forecast inputs, KPI governance, and the operating rules that make dashboards useful.

That is the layer I have spent much of my career building. At QXO, I connected CRM, marketing automation, internal customer databases, credit workflows, review data, call-center activity, and analytics into one commercial pipeline. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I can augment an internal RevOps team with commercial architecture, data design, segmentation, forecasting, dashboards, and hands-on implementation capacity.

I would welcome 20 minutes to compare your current roadmap with the work we have already operationalized elsewhere. My approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$,
  email_follow_up_1 = $$Hi Helene,

A focused starting point could be a commercial-systems diagnostic covering lifecycle stages, source-of-truth logic, account and territory rules, forecast governance, dashboard ownership, and the activation rules connecting insight to GTM action.

The output would be a prioritized build plan your team could execute directly or use us to accelerate. Would a short conversation next week be worthwhile?$$,
  email_follow_up_2 = $$Hi Helene,

I know this likely competes with a long RevOps backlog, so I will keep this simple. We are most useful where the business knows the decisions it needs to make but the data, definitions, and cross-functional ownership are not yet aligned.

Would you be open to a 20-minute working session, or should I connect with someone else on the team?$$,
  email_assumption_notice = $$Assumed from the first-initial-plus-last-name pattern demonstrated by tsmith@restaurant365.com. This email may not work and should be verified before sending.$$
where lower(contact_name) = lower('Helene Hartmann-Dirani') and company = 'Restaurant365';

update public.project_contacts set
  linkedin_connect_message = $$Hi Tony, R365's focus on connecting restaurant financial and operating data into clearer decisions strongly aligns with the commercial systems work I lead. I help companies create the same connected view across growth, customers, and revenue. I would value connecting.$$,
  intro_message = $$Thanks for connecting, Tony. Based on your work as Co-Founder and Chief Executive Officer at Restaurant365, I wanted to be direct about why I reached out. RevHub helps organizations connect customer and market intelligence, segmentation, pricing, marketing, sales execution, operations, forecasting and executive reporting into one commercial growth system. For Restaurant365, the opportunity I see is: RevHub can help Tony apply R365's connected-data philosophy internally by unifying commercial intelligence, growth priorities, revenue forecasting, customer lifecycle performance, and executive reporting. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss what we do and whether it could support your priorities?$$,
  follow_up_message = $$Hi Tony, following up in case my earlier note got buried. I outlined the commercial growth approach behind RevHub here: https://aboutchad.com/approach. Based on your role at Restaurant365, I believe there may be a relevant opportunity around founder-ceo scaling a $100m-plus restaurant technology company through ai, market expansion, new executive hires, and a platform promise centered on connected financial and operational data. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss the approach and whether it could be useful to your team?$$,
  email_subject = $$Applying R365's connected-data model to the commercial engine$$,
  email_intro_message = $$Hi Tony,

Restaurant365's core promise is replacing disconnected restaurant systems with a clearer operating view. I believe there is a parallel opportunity inside the commercial engine: connect market and customer intelligence, acquisition, sales, implementation, adoption, retention, expansion, and forecasting into one management model.

I have spent more than 15 years building commercial growth systems across marketing, revenue operations, analytics, and activation. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while connecting fragmented CRM, marketing, customer, credit, call-center, and operational systems. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I bring both the commercial strategy and data depth needed to accelerate this work without adding several isolated hires.

For R365, I would begin with a commercial control layer that shows where growth is created, where value realization slows, and which interventions have the greatest revenue impact by restaurant segment.

Would you be open to 20 minutes next week? My approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$,
  email_follow_up_1 = $$Hi Tony,

One useful outcome from an initial engagement would be a leadership-ready view connecting acquisition, pipeline, implementation, product adoption, retention, and expansion to segment economics. That would help the team prioritize growth investments and operating improvements from the same evidence.

Would Tuesday or Thursday work for a brief conversation?$$,
  email_follow_up_2 = $$Hi Tony,

Closing the loop. The reason I reached out is that R365 already understands the value of connected operational data. RevHub applies that same principle to the system responsible for creating and expanding revenue.

I would be glad to share the first-30-days framework in a short conversation. Is there a time worth holding?$$,
  email_assumption_notice = $$Verified public business email.$$
where lower(contact_name) = lower('Tony Smith') and company = 'Restaurant365';

update public.project_contacts set
  linkedin_connect_message = $$Hi Eric, your move to R365 and focus on scaling operations, customer value, automation, and AI caught my attention. I build commercial operating systems that connect customer signals, growth execution, and executive visibility. I would value connecting.$$,
  intro_message = $$Thanks for connecting, Eric. Based on your work as Chief Operating Officer at Restaurant365, I wanted to be direct about why I reached out. RevHub helps organizations connect customer and market intelligence, segmentation, pricing, marketing, sales execution, operations, forecasting and executive reporting into one commercial growth system. For Restaurant365, the opportunity I see is: RevHub can help Eric connect commercial planning, customer adoption, operational performance, and revenue outcomes into a shared operating cadence across the expanding R365 platform. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss what we do and whether it could support your priorities?$$,
  follow_up_message = $$Hi Eric, following up in case my earlier note got buried. I outlined the commercial growth approach behind RevHub here: https://aboutchad.com/approach. Based on your role at Restaurant365, I believe there may be a relevant opportunity around new coo charged with scaling operations, customer value, automation, ai, and the company's next phase of growth. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss the approach and whether it could be useful to your team?$$,
  email_subject = $$A commercial operating model for R365's next phase$$,
  email_intro_message = $$Hi Eric,

Your mandate at Restaurant365 sits where growth strategy, customer value, operations, automation, and AI have to become one repeatable system. That usually requires more than separate marketing, sales, customer-success, and analytics workstreams. Leadership needs a shared operating model connecting demand, sales, implementation effort, adoption, support demand, retention, expansion, and unit economics.

I have built these systems across complex organizations for more than 15 years. At QXO, I helped connect fragmented customer, marketing, credit, call-center, and operational data while scaling digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I combine commercial strategy, process design, analytics, forecasting, and implementation.

For R365, an initial diagnostic could identify where growth creates operating strain, where customers stall before realizing value, and which interventions deserve executive priority.

Would you be open to 20 minutes next week? My approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$,
  email_follow_up_1 = $$Hi Eric,

A practical first step would connect the full customer lifecycle to operating economics: acquisition, sales cycle, implementation effort, activation, support demand, retention, and expansion. That view often surfaces the few process or product changes that can improve both growth and customer value.

Would a brief working session next week be useful?$$,
  email_follow_up_2 = $$Hi Eric,

I wanted to close the loop. We are most useful when a company has strong leaders and systems but needs a connective operating layer across growth, customer value, and execution.

I can share a concise diagnostic structure in 20 minutes. Is there a window worth holding, or a better owner for this conversation?$$,
  email_assumption_notice = $$Assumed from the first-initial-plus-last-name pattern demonstrated by tsmith@restaurant365.com. This email may not work and should be verified before sending.$$
where lower(contact_name) = lower('Eric Cox') and company = 'Restaurant365';

