update public.project_contacts set
  linkedin_connect_message = $$Hi Allyns, I saw HR Transformed's search for fractional Chief Marketing and Growth leadership. The mandate to connect positioning, acquisition, conversion, retention, B2B expansion, and trustworthy measurement closely matches commercial growth systems I have built. I would value connecting.$$,
  intro_message = $$Thanks for connecting, Allyns. Based on your work as Chief Executive Officer and Founder at HR Transformed, I wanted to be direct about why I reached out. RevHub helps organizations connect customer and market intelligence, segmentation, pricing, marketing, sales execution, operations, forecasting and executive reporting into one commercial growth system. For HR Transformed, the opportunity I see is: Chad can help Allyns build a practical commercial growth system around HR Transformed's existing authority in outsourced HR, coaching, compliance, and people strategy, connecting positioning, audience segmentation, demand generation, client lifecycle, CRM, attribution, forecasting, and executive reporting without requiring several separate hires. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss what we do and whether it could support your priorities?$$,
  follow_up_message = $$Hi Allyns, following up in case my earlier note got buried. I outlined the commercial growth approach behind RevHub here: https://aboutchad.com/approach. Based on your role at HR Transformed, I believe there may be a relevant opportunity around hr transformed is seeking fractional chief marketing and growth leadership to connect brand, acquisition, conversion, retention, b2b expansion, segmentation, attribution, dashboards, and revenue optimization. as founder and ceo, allyns is the clear executive owner of the mandate and the only publicly verified leader at the appropriate seniority. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss the approach and whether it could be useful to your team?$$,
  email_subject = $$Building HR Transformed's next repeatable growth system$$,
  email_intro_message = $$Hi Allyns,

I saw HR Transformed's search for fractional Chief Marketing and Growth leadership. What stood out is the breadth of the mandate: brand, acquisition, conversion, retention, B2B expansion, segmentation, attribution, dashboards, and revenue optimization. That is not simply a marketing hire. It is the buildout of a connected commercial growth system.

I have spent more than 15 years creating those systems across positioning, customer segmentation, demand generation, CRM, lifecycle orchestration, forecasting, analytics, and executive reporting. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while connecting fragmented CRM, marketing, customer, call-center, and operational data into one usable growth model. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I bring both the strategy and analytical depth needed to move quickly without requiring HR Transformed to assemble several separate specialists.

For HR Transformed, I would begin by identifying the highest-value client segments, sharpening the growth narrative for each, mapping the journey from awareness through consultation and recurring engagement, and establishing one measurement model for acquisition, conversion, retention, and expansion.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation next week? My approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$,
  email_follow_up_1 = $$Hi Allyns,

One practical first deliverable would be a commercial growth map connecting each priority client segment to its buying trigger, value proposition, entry channel, consultation path, service mix, retention signals, and expansion opportunities. That would make it easier to see where growth is constrained by audience, message, process, or measurement.

Would a brief conversation next week be worthwhile?$$,
  email_follow_up_2 = $$Hi Allyns,

Closing the loop. HR Transformed already has strong credibility and client proof. The opportunity I see is turning that foundation into a more predictable system for demand, conversion, recurring engagement, and executive visibility.

I would be glad to share a concise first-30-days framework in 20 minutes. Is there a time worth holding?$$,
  email_assumption_notice = $$Verified public business email published on HR Transformed's official website.$$
where lower(contact_name) = lower('Allyns Melendez, MBA') and company = 'HR Transformed';

