update public.project_contacts set
  linkedin_connect_message = $$Hi Amanda, your work taking BleuBully from a product idea to a sold-out D2C brand caught my attention. I build commercial systems across segmentation, lifecycle, analytics, forecasting, and revenue operations, and would value connecting and comparing approaches.$$,
  intro_message = $$Thanks for connecting, Amanda. Based on your work as Fractional CMO, BleuBully Bedding; Founder and CEO, MOD Consulting at BleuBully Bedding, I wanted to be direct about why I reached out. RevHub helps organizations connect customer and market intelligence, segmentation, pricing, marketing, sales execution, operations, forecasting and executive reporting into one commercial growth system. For BleuBully Bedding, the opportunity I see is: Chad and Harsh can complement Amanda with deeper commercial architecture, customer and channel analytics, lifecycle economics, forecasting, CRM governance, and executive reporting so BleuBully can scale the brand without turning the next growth phase into disconnected campaigns or systems. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss what we do and whether it could support your priorities?$$,
  follow_up_message = $$Hi Amanda, following up in case my earlier note got buried. I outlined the commercial growth approach behind RevHub here: https://aboutchad.com/approach. Based on your role at BleuBully Bedding, I believe there may be a relevant opportunity around bleubully is seeking fractional cmo leadership while expanding a sold-out premium bedding concept into a broader d2c collection, new colors, wholesale opportunities, retention programs, and disciplined growth measurement. amanda has already helped build the brand, pricing, positioning, website, email flows, launch, and demand engine, placing her at the same seniority as the mandate and closest to the current commercial challenges. Would you be open to a quick 15-minute call to discuss the approach and whether it could be useful to your team?$$,
  email_subject = $$A commercial operating layer for BleuBully's next stage$$,
  email_intro_message = $$Hi Amanda,

Your work taking BleuBully from a product idea to a sold-out D2C brand stood out. The next phase appears materially different from launch: product and color expansion, acquisition efficiency, website conversion, lifecycle growth, wholesale opportunities, inventory decisions, and a clearer view of contribution economics.

I have spent more than 15 years building commercial systems that connect customer segmentation, campaigns, CRM, lifecycle behavior, forecasting, analytics, and executive reporting. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while unifying fragmented customer, marketing, call-center, and operational data. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I add the strategy and analytical depth needed to turn growth activity into a shared operating model.

For BleuBully, a practical first step could connect audience and creative tests to first-order margin, product affinity, repeat purchase, wholesale potential, and inventory implications. That would help clarify which customer and channel patterns are worth scaling as the assortment expands.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation to compare approaches? Our framework is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$,
  email_follow_up_1 = $$Hi Amanda,

One concrete deliverable could be a customer and channel growth map connecting acquisition source, creative message, first purchase, product mix, margin, repeat behavior, and wholesale potential. It would show where BleuBully is generating durable customer value versus short-term demand.

Would a brief conversation next week be useful?$$,
  email_follow_up_2 = $$Hi Amanda,

Closing the loop. BleuBully already has the brand story and early market proof. The opportunity I see is building the commercial measurement and decision system that helps the team scale acquisition, retention, assortment, and wholesale from the same evidence.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding, or is another stakeholder closer to that work?$$,
  email_assumption_notice = $$Verified public business email published by Amanda Pond in a LinkedIn post for MOD Consulting. This is Amanda's consulting-company address, not a BleuBully company-domain email.$$
where lower(contact_name) = lower('Amanda Pond') and company = 'BleuBully Bedding';

